    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 11 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Be the first to get rid of all your cards: first your hand, then your four face-up table cards, then your four face-down mystery cards. Each deal has one winner; the overall game is won by the player with the lowest cumulative score when someone reaches 500 points.',
      'Turn-flow example: Players take turns adding one to four cards of the same rank to the centre play pile. Cards played must be equal to or lower than the top card; if higher, the player must pick up the whole pile first then play. A 10 or Joker clears the pile (swoop) and the player gets an extra turn. Four of a kind on top also clears the pile (swoop) and grants an extra turn. Mystery cards are played only as the first card of a turn; the player flips one face up and must play it immediately. First to empty hand, then face-up cards, then mystery cards wins the deal.',
      'Scoring example: When one player runs out of cards, others total points in hand (A=1, 2-9 face value, J/Q/K=10, 10/Joker=50). Cumulative; game ends when any player reaches 500+. Lowest score wins. Empty Hand, then Face-Up, then Mystery. First to do so wins the deal; game winner is lowest cumulative score when someone reaches 500+..',
